        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An 18V drill and a 20V MAX drill run on the same five-cell battery. One label quotes the average working voltage and the other quotes the peak, and neither tells you which drill is stronger. Motor type, electronics, gearing and battery size decide performance, and the battery platform decides what every future tool will cost you.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            So choose the platform first: stay with the batteries you own, or pick the system with the tools you want next. Then buy the best drill on that platform your budget allows, ideally brushless and with two batteries. Our cordless drill rankings cover the strongest options under both labels.
          </p>
        </div>

